<p>If <code>x</code> is a NaN, a NaN is returned.</p>
<p>If <code>x</code> is +0 (-0), +0 (-0) is returned.</p>
<p>If <code>x</code> is positive infinity, positive infinity is
returned.</p>
<p>If <code>x</code> is less than -0, a domain error occurs, and a NaN is
returned.</p>
